---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: author.name,
    section: "Brand Reviews",
    tags: [
      "happy viking protein powder",
      "happy viking protein",
      "happy viking review",
      "venus williams protein powder"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{
    text: "See Our Top Plant Protein Picks",
    link: "/best-plant-based-protein-powder/",
  }}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #38BDF8 0, transparent 45%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 60%, #FF4500 0, transparent 40%);"></div>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF4500]/20 text-[#FF4500] text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest border border-[#FF4500]/30">
            Brand Review
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
            Label-Checked
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          Happy Viking Protein <span class="text-[#38BDF8]">Powder</span> Review
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          Venus Williams' Happy Viking is a vegan meal shake with 30 g of protein and 10 g of fiber after its 2025 reformulation. Here is what is in it, which listings still sell the old formula, and what each gram of protein costs.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="#happy-viking-plant-protein-triple-chocolate"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
          >
            See Our #1 Pick
          </a>
          <a
            href="#old-vs-new"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
          >
            Read the Verdict
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <AuthorAvatar size={48} />
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">{author.name}</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">{author.role}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 hidden sm:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Last Updated</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">{dates.display}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block ml-auto">
          <SocialProof />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#verdict" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">1. The Short Verdict</a>
          <a href="#the-brand" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">2. Who Makes Happy Viking</a>
          <a href="#label" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">3. The Label, Line by Line</a>
          <a href="#top-picks" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">4. Our Top Picks</a>
          <a href="#old-vs-new" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">5. Old 20 g vs New 30 g Formula</a>
          <a href="#cost-per-25g" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">6. Cost per 25 g of Protein</a>
          <a href="#meal-vs-protein" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">7. Meal Shake or Protein Powder?</a>
          <a href="#additives" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">8. Sweeteners, Ashwagandha and Testing</a>
          <a href="#who-should-skip" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">9. Who Should Skip It</a>
          <a href="#vs-rivals" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">10. Happy Viking vs the Rivals</a>
          <a href="#mistakes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">11. Common Mistakes</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">12. FAQ</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Happy Viking is a solid vegan meal replacement and an expensive protein powder. Per the brand's label at the time of writing, two scoops of the reformulated Everyday Bag give 30 g of pea and brown rice protein, 10 g of fiber and about 250 calories, with 5 g of added cane sugar, MCT oil, probiotics and ashwagandha. At about $60 for 15 servings, that is roughly $3 to $3.40 per 25 g of protein, so buy it to replace a meal, not to top up protein after training.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="verdict" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. The Short Verdict
          </h2>

          <p>
            Happy Viking is good at what it now claims to be: a vegan meal replacement. The reformulated shake delivers 30 g of protein from yellow pea and brown rice, 10 g of fiber, healthy fats from MCT oil, and a long list of vitamins, minerals and plant extracts, in about 250 calories per two-scoop serving. As a quick breakfast or a lunch you drink at your desk, that is a well-built profile.
          </p>

          <p>
            It is much less convincing as a protein powder. At about $60 for a 15-serving bag, you are paying roughly $3 to $3.40 for every 25 g of protein, two to three times the cost of a plain pea or pea and rice protein. You are also getting 5 g of added cane sugar, 6 g of saturated fat and an adaptogen with every scoop, which you may not want in a simple post-workout shake.
          </p>

          <p>
            The one trap to avoid is buying the old formula. Amazon still lists 20 g single-serve packs from before the 2025 relaunch alongside the new 30 g bags and packs. Check that the title says 30 g of protein before you buy. The Triple Chocolate Everyday Bag is the product to start with, and our <a href="/best-plant-based-protein-powder/">plant-based protein powder rankings</a> cover cheaper plant proteins if you only need the protein.
          </p>

          <p>
            In short: buy Happy Viking if you want a vegan meal shake with more protein and fiber than most, and you are happy with a little added sugar. Skip it if you want the cheapest plant protein per gram, a sugar-free shake, or a certified product for drug-tested sport.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-3">THE VERDICT</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">A strong vegan meal shake, an expensive protein powder.</p>
            <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed m-0">Buy the 30 g Triple Chocolate Everyday Bag to replace a meal. If you want protein for training, a plain pea and rice blend gives you the same grams for half the price or less.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="the-brand" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. Who Makes Happy Viking
          </h2>

          <p>
            Happy Viking was created by tennis champion Venus Williams, who says on the brand's site that plant-based, high-protein nutrition helped her manage an autoimmune disease and recover as an athlete. The brand lists investors including golfer Michelle Wie West and soccer player Megan Rapinoe. Celebrity founders are common in this category, and Williams has been unusually public about following a mostly plant-based diet for years, which gives the product a credible origin story.
          </p>

          <p>
            The product has changed significantly. Earlier versions were sold as a 20 g plant protein shake, including ready-to-drink bottles and single-serve powder packs. In late 2025 the brand relaunched the powder around what it calls a 30 and 10 formula, 30 g of protein and 10 g of fiber per serving, removed erythritol and repositioned the product as a complete meal replacement with more than 100 superfoods, vitamins and minerals.
          </p>

          <p>
            Today the core product is the Everyday Bag, a resealable bag of about 15 two-scoop servings, plus 12-count boxes of single-serve travel packs and smaller sampler packs. Flavors at the time of writing include Triple Chocolate, Vanilla Bean, Strawberry and Berry Parfait, with travel-pack flavors such as Cookies and Cream, Greena Colada, and coffee latte versions that the brand says contain about 80 mg of caffeine.
          </p>

          <p>
            Happy Viking sells direct through its own site, with a 10 percent subscription discount and a 30-day money-back guarantee per the brand, and on Amazon, where both the new Everyday Bags and older single-serve packs are listed. We have not tasted or tested it. Taste and texture notes in this review are buyer feedback, and nutrition figures come from the brand's labels and Amazon listings.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="label" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. The Label, Line by Line
          </h2>

          <p>
            The Triple Chocolate label is the one we could read in full on the brand's site at the time of writing. A two-scoop serving of about 63 g, mixed into 16 oz of liquid, lists the figures below. The brand recommends almond or oat milk, which will add calories and, with soy or pea milk, more protein. The other flavors' panels on the brand page sit within a few calories and grams of these figures.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Per 2 scoops (63 g)</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Triple Chocolate</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">What it means</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Calories</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 250</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">A light meal, before milk</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Protein</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">30 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Yellow pea and brown rice</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Fiber</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">10 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Acacia, guar and other sources</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Total and added sugar</td>
